   - A cutoff at 13.4 kHz is typical of an MP3/AAC at 96 kbps or less.
   - Above the cutoff there is digital silence: nothing was added after the encoder, so a lossy file was converted back to a lossless format.
   - Encoder holes of 43 dB below the 13.4 kHz lowpass: the fingerprint of a perceptual encoder (MP3, MP2, AAC). FM and analog recordings stay under about 5 dB.
   - High frequencies are present (-0 dB relative to 1-4 kHz above 15 kHz), so encoder traces would show.
